  "slug": "gland-development-mll4-4b67",
  "summary": "New long-read methylation tools and large-scale transcriptomic decompositions aim to disentangle cell-type mixture effects from intrinsic state shifts.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is separating changes in cell-type composition from changes within cells. COMET assigns bulk long-read DNA reads to cell types using cell-type-specific methylation, separating composition shifts from within-cell changes in blood, brain and other tissues. LongReadClock applies the same logic to ageing, building cell-type-resolved epigenetic clocks from bulk blood long-read methylation data. At larger scale, a single-cell foundation model (UCE) spanning more than 59M cells across 614 states maps state bridges and composition remodeling. Robust multi-run ICA of 778 CHO RNA-seq samples yields 105 reproducible iModulons capturing lineage, stress and process-responsive states. Related work reports a small germ-layer imprint on transcriptomic ageing across 24 GTEx tissues, distinct multi-omic effects of individual CHIP driver genes, mucociliary programs in healthy endocervix and ectocervix, and a 12-gene neuroimmune signature in HPV-associated cervical cancer. What is new is the use of long-read methylation to resolve cell types directly from bulk samples. All findings remain preprint observations.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
